builder/generated/
# Local git worktrees used by the sprint workflow
.worktrees/
# Worktrees created by Claude Code agents (isolation: worktree)
.claude/worktrees/

# Runtime SQLite stores (registry + native calendar). Both default to living
# under DATA_DIR, but bot/registry-db.js and bot/calendar-native/db.js fall
# back to writing next to their own source file when DATA_DIR is unset — e.g.
# running the server locally from bot/ without DATA_DIR creates bot/registry.sqlite
# right there. This is exactly how bot/registry.sqlite ended up committed on
# main (see HANDOFF-docs.md) — ignore the pattern everywhere so it can't
# happen again, including WAL/SHM/journal sidecars.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal

# QA evidence: never commit regenerable, multi-MB proof-of-flow artifacts.
# See AGENTS.md "Repository weight — QA evidence policy" for what belongs
# here instead (small capped screenshots + a findings/summary manifest).
# `git add -f` still works for the rare evidence file that genuinely needs
# to be tracked — this is a default, not a hard block.
04-QA-Evidence/**/export.html
04-QA-Evidence/**/export.zip
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.webm
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.mp4
04-Deliverables/**/*.webm
04-Deliverables/**/*.mp4

# QA evidence screenshots are regenerated by the oracles on every run. Only the
# final round is kept in the repository; everything else refills locally as a
# transient artifact and must never be committed again. (2026-09-07: 1120 such
# files had accumulated to 705MB.)
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.png
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.jpg
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.jpeg
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.webp
04-QA-Evidence/**/*.gif
!04-QA-Evidence/Final/**
